# Low-Cost Air Isolator

**An open, low-cost, latex-free breath/sensor isolator for sip-and-puff assistive devices.**

A few-cent, latex-free, user-replaceable membrane that fully separates a user's breath (saliva, moisture, pathogens) from the pressure sensor and electronics of a sip-and-puff (breath-actuated) assistive switch — giving both **sensor protection** and **between-user hygiene**. It's designed for 3D printing plus common medical consumables (a nitrile finger cot as the membrane), and is meant to be reused across open-source assistive-technology projects.

![Screw-together Unit — concept schematic](./air-isolator-screw-unit.svg)

> **Status: working prototype (V0.1), preliminary.** It screws together and seems to work well in early hands-on use, but it is **not validated**. We are actively seeking testing, food-safety review, and improvements — **from experts, makers, and users alike**. This is **not** a certified medical device (see [Disclaimer](#disclaimer)).

