## Quick start (print one)

1. **Pick your tube size** (1/4" recommended for printability, strength, and comfort) and print the matching pair from [`/stl`](./stl) — e.g. `...FrontShell_-_V0_1_-_25in_Tube.stl` + `...RearShell_-_V0_1_-_25in_Tube.stl`. PETG, or transparent food-grade PCTG for the mouthpiece; a stainless/hardened-steel nozzle is recommended.
2. Seat a **nitrile finger cot** (latex-free) as the membrane, slack — not stretched.
3. **Screw the two shells together** to clamp the cot cuff at the seam (that forms the seal — no glue).
4. Push the barbed spigot into your sensor tube.

See the [fabrication brief](./AirIsolator_Fabrication_Brief.pdf) and [design note](./air-isolator.md) for materials, food safety, and hygiene.

## Measured specs (V0)

| Part | Bounding box | Mass (PETG) | Watertight? |
|---|---|---|---|
| Front shell V0.1 (same for both tube sizes) | 34 × 34 × 63 mm | ~11.8 g | Yes |
| Rear shell V0.1 — 1/4" tube | 32 × 32 × 68 mm | ~14.1 g | Yes |
| Rear shell V0.1 — 1/8" tube | 32 × 32 × 61 mm | ~12.6 g \* | **No** \* |
| Combined (1/4" build) | — | ~26 g (~8.5 m filament) | — |

\* The **1/8" rear shell mesh isn't yet watertight**, so its figures are estimates; the **1/4" rear shell is watertight**. See the [prototype note](./air-isolator-prototype-v1.md). (The two front-shell files are geometrically identical — the tube size only changes the rear shell.)

## Food safety & hygiene

The mouthpiece is mouth-adjacent, but the **membrane and tubing are the actual hygienic barrier**, so the printed surface is a second-line concern. Baseline plan: treat the mouthpiece as a small, cheap **disposable** in food-grade filament, hand-washed and replaced on schedule (nothing printed is dishwasher-safe). Optional epoxy/silicone finishes and a biocompatible-SLA route are documented in the [design note](./air-isolator.md#mouthpiece-hygiene-strategy).

## Feedback & contributing

We'd love feedback from **anyone with relevant expertise**, from **other open-source assistive-device makers**, and above all from **people who use assistive devices**.

- **Open an [Issue](https://github.com/mkadie/LowCostAirIsolator/issues) or Discussion** — preferred; keeps it public and iterable.
- **Pull requests welcome** — STL/design improvements, docs, or test data.
- Email: main@tssfaa.com

See [`air-isolator-prototype-v1.md`](./air-isolator-prototype-v1.md) for the specific questions we're hoping experts can help with.

